# SHIPPED-SURFACE — the harness's shipped surface, AS DATA (agent-infra#1960).
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS. The one place that says, in reviewable text, which files under
# scripts/orchestrator-harness/ a deployment at $O is supposed to receive. Three programs read it and
# none of them keeps its own copy of the answer:
#
#   install.sh                 records a per-file content hash of every shipped path in
#                              $O/.agent-infra-stamp.json ("shippedFiles" + "shippedFileCount"),
#                              taken from the SOURCE tree — never from the deployment.
#   check-deployed-drift.sh    reads this file AT THE REF and requires every shipped path to be
#                              present in $O with the ref's bytes; a missing one is named MISSING.
#   harness.sh deploy          mirrors exactly this list into $O and removes what it no longer names.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS EXISTS — the defect it removes. Until 2026-10-18 the deployed-bytes record covered
# `$O/*.sh` and nothing else: a `grep -E '^…/[^/]+\.sh$'` over the ref's tree. Measured on the laptop
# the same day: `$O/gh-limit.py` was ABSENT from the live deployment while present on origin/main, and
# the record never saw it, because a `.py` is not a `.sh`. `$O/gh-rest/gh:102` resolves
# `$SELF_DIR/../gh-limit.py`; without it the shim printed
#   `gh-rest: WARNING no limit layer … this call was NOT serialised or backed off (#1988)`
# and fell back to the raw binary, which then failed outright (`GraphQL: API rate limit already
# exceeded` while REST reported `graphql 4537/5000` remaining). Every `gh issue view` / `gh pr list`
# was refused → pre-flight DEGRADED/INCOMPLETE for every candidate → `refresh-candidates.sh` aborts by
# design (#1736) → `candidates.txt` stayed 0 lines for 4.5 h → `[dispatch] backlog empty queue=READ(203)`
# with 200 issues open and 19 of 20 lane slots free. A filter is not a record: a glob can only cover
# the kinds of file its author happened to think of, and every kind it does not name is invisible
# BY CONSTRUCTION — the record then reports a MATCH over a deployment that is missing files.
#
# ⛔ THE RULE, AND WHY IT IS AN ALLOWLIST OF PATHS RATHER THAN OF EXTENSIONS. Every file in this
# directory ships UNLESS it is named below with a leading `!`. A new file added to the tree is
# therefore NOT covered by default: `check-deployed-drift.sh` compares the ref's tree against THIS
# FILE and reports any tree file that is neither shipped nor declared not-shipped. That is the one
# place the incompleteness of this list can be seen, and it is a red deployment, not a silence.
# Extensions would have been shorter and would have re-created the defect the first time someone
# shipped a `.json`, a `.toml`, or an extensionless bin shim.
#
# FORMAT — one path per line, relative to this directory:
#   <path>        ships: deploy copies it to $O/<path> and the record must name it
#   !<path>       does NOT ship. <path> may end in `/` to cover a whole directory.
#   # …           comment. Blank lines ignored.
# Keep this file sorted within its groups.
#
